# Atlas MCP Design Controls

<!-- merged from: atlas/30-atlas-mcp-design-controls + leo/atlas-control-author (rule entry point) -->

The `user-atlas-design-controls` MCP server is the sole source of truth for design controls. See `mcp-sole-source.mdc` for the binding lock-in.

## Authentication

Cursor on macOS does not load `~/.zprofile`, so MCP bearer tokens cannot rely on shell `export`.

```bash
python3 tools/atlas-mcp-auth/login.py login
```

Restart Cursor after login. Refresh expired tokens with:

```bash
python3 tools/atlas-mcp-auth/login.py refresh
```

## When to use which tool

| Trigger | Tool to call |
|---|---|
| Before modifying a Class B/C DI | `get_change_impact` |
| Before implementing any DC | `get_traceability_gaps` |
| After implementing a DO | `link_work_item` |
| After automated tests pass | `ingest_ci_evidence` |
| Reading a specific DC | `get_design_control` or `atlas://design-controls/{type}/{id}` |
| Creating / updating an Initiative | `create_initiative`, `update_initiative` |
| Creating / updating a Release | `create_release`, `update_release` |
| Recording a Release gate decision | `record_release_gate_decision` |
| Creating / updating a Design Review | `create_design_review`, `update_design_review` |
| Recording a DR decision | `record_design_review_decision` |

## Canonical graph directions

| Field | Relationship | Direction |
|---|---|---|
| `userNeeds.linkedToDI` | `HAS_DESIGN_INPUT` | UN → DI |
| `designInputs.linkedToDO` | `IMPLEMENTS` | DO → DI (incoming to DI) |
| `designInputs.linkedToVT` | `VERIFIES` | VT → DI (incoming to DI) |
| `designOutputs.linkedToVT` | `TESTS` | VT → DO (incoming to DO) |
| `validationTests.linkedToUN` | `VALIDATES` | VAL → UN |
| `risks.linkedToDI` | `MITIGATES` | DI → Risk (incoming to Risk) |

## Search before create

For every artefact type, call `search_design_controls(query=..., dc_type=...)` first. Inspect near-matches with `get_design_control`. Prefer update over create.

## Write tool permissions

Write tools require `qa-ra-lead`, `developer`, or `admin` role. If you get a permission error, contact your QMS admin.

## Local dev (no token needed)

```bash
cd services/mcp-design-controls
DEBUG=true QMS_GRAPH_API_URL=http://localhost:8032 uvicorn app.main:app --port 8040 --reload
```
